  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.57,
            0.047,
            0.847,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Tale of Three Intersecting Lines"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.605,
            0.107
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does everything look right with this triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.107,
            0.848,
            0.162
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If this triangle were possible, then the direct path between any two vertices should be shorter than the roundabout path via the third vertex. Is this true for our rough diagram?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.162,
            0.603,
            0.181
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us consider the paths between B and C."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.186,
            0.492,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Direct path length = BC = 10 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.211,
            0.847,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the length of the roundabout path via the vertex A? It is the sum of the lengths of line segments BA and AC."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.254,
            0.764,
            0.274
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roundabout path length = BA + AC = 15 cm + 30 cm = 45 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.279,
            0.846,
            0.317
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the direct path length shorter than the roundabout path length? Yes. Let us now consider the paths between A and B."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.322,
            0.493,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Direct path length = AB = 15 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.551,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.346,
            0.832,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Finding the length of the roundabout path via the vertex C, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.371,
            0.763,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roundabout path length = AC + CB = 30 cm + 10 cm = 40 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.395,
            0.846,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the direct path length shorter than the roundabout path length? Yes. Finally, consider paths between C and A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.439,
            0.492,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Direct path length = CA = 30 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.464,
            0.762,
            0.484
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Roundabout path length = CB + BA = 10 cm + 15 cm = 25 cm"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.489,
            0.847,
            0.544
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is the direct path length shorter than the roundabout path length? In this case, the direct path is longer, which is absurd. Can such a triangle exist? No."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.544,
            0.847,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Therefore, a triangle having sidelengths 10 cm, 15 cm and 30 cm cannot exist."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.581,
            0.848,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We are thus able to see without construction why a triangle for the set of lengths 10 cm, 15 cm and 30 cm cannot exist. We have been able to figure this out through spatial intuition and reasoning."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.637,
            0.848,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Recall how we used similar intuition and reasoning to discover properties of intersecting and parallel lines. We will continue to do this as we explore geometry."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.701,
            0.847,
            0.723
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can we say anything about the existence of a triangle having sidelengths"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.722,
            0.727,
            0.742
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3 cm, 3 cm and 7 cm? Verify your answer by construction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.761,
            0.73,
            0.839
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? “In the rough diagram in Fig. 7.4, is it possible to assign lengths in a different order such that the direct paths are always coming out to be shorter than the roundabout paths? If this is possible, then a triangle might exist.”"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.844,
            0.724,
            0.869
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Is such rearrangement of lengths possible in the triangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
